{"1-2":{"people":[{"id":"phoebe-g5402","name":"Phoebe","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[{"id":"cenchreae-g2747","name":"Cenchreae","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"words":[{"base":"G2747","lemma":"Κεγχρεαί","tr":"Kegchreai","gloss":"Cenchreae","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G5535","lemma":"χρῄζω","tr":"chrēzō","gloss":"to need","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G0516","lemma":"ἀξίως","tr":"axiōs","gloss":"appropriately","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G4229","lemma":"πρᾶγμα","tr":"pragma","gloss":"thing","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"G4327","lemma":"προσδέχομαι","tr":"prosdechomai","gloss":"to wait for","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"G4921","lemma":"συνίστημι, συνιστάω","tr":"sunistēmi, sunistaō","gloss":"to commend","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"G0079","lemma":"ἀδελφή","tr":"adelphē","gloss":"sister","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":26},{"base":"G1249","lemma":"διάκονος","tr":"diakonos","gloss":"servant","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":29},{"base":"G3936","lemma":"παρίστημι","tr":"paristēmi","gloss":"to stand by","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":41},{"base":"G1577","lemma":"ἐκκλησία","tr":"ekklēsia","gloss":"assembly","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":114}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PHP","chapter":2,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Welcome him in the Lord with great joy, and honor men like him,","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":18,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Paul remained in Corinth for quite some time before saying goodbye to the brothers. He had his head shaved in Cenchrea to keep a vow he had made, and then he sailed for Syria, accompanied by Priscilla and Aquila.","from":1},{"book":"MAT","chapter":10,"verse":40,"verseEnd":42,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"He who receives you receives Me, and he who receives Me receives the One who sent Me. Whoever receives a prophet because he is a prophet will receive a prophetʼs reward, and whoever receives a righteous man because he is a righteous man will receive a righteous manʼs reward. And if anyone gives even a cup of cold water to one of these little ones because he is My disciple, truly I tell you, he will never lose his reward.”","from":2},{"book":"MAT","chapter":12,"verse":50,"verseEnd":50,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"For whoever does the will of My Father in heaven is My brother and sister and mother.”","from":1},{"book":"MAT","chapter":25,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the King will reply, ‘Truly I tell you, whatever you did for one of the least of these brothers of Mine, you did for Me.’","from":2},{"book":"MRK","chapter":10,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"will fail to receive a hundredfold in the present age—houses and brothers and sisters and mothers and children and fields, along with persecutions—and in the age to come, eternal life.","from":1},{"book":"LUK","chapter":8,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Joanna the wife of Herodʼs household manager Chuza, Susanna, and many others. These women were ministering to them out of their own means.","from":1},{"book":"ACT","chapter":9,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In Joppa there was a disciple named Tabitha (which is translated as Dorcas), who was always occupied with works of kindness and charity.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2}]},"3-16":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":6,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"aquila-g0207","name":"Aquila","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"priscilla-g4252","name":"Priscilla","kind":"person","brief":"Christian teacher","count":1,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"epaenetus-g1866","name":"Epaenetus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"mary-g3137m","name":"Mary","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"andronicus-g0408","name":"Andronicus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"junia-g2458","name":"Junia","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"ampliatus-g0291","name":"Ampliatus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"stachys-g4720","name":"Stachys","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"urbanus-g3773","name":"Urbanus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"apelles-g0559","name":"Apelles","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"aristobulus-g0711","name":"Aristobulus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"herodion-g2267","name":"Herodion","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"narcissus-g3488","name":"Narcissus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"persis-g4069","name":"Persis","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"tryphaena-g5170","name":"Tryphaena","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"tryphosa-g5173","name":"Tryphosa","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"rufus-g4504h","name":"Rufus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"asyncritus-g0799","name":"Asyncritus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"hermas-g2057","name":"Hermas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"hermes-g2060h","name":"Hermes","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"patrobas-g3969","name":"Patrobas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"phlegon-g5393","name":"Phlegon","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"julia-g2456","name":"Julia","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"nereus-g3517","name":"Nereus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"olympas-g3652","name":"Olympas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"philologus-g5378","name":"Philologus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15}],"places":[{"id":"achaia-g0882","name":"Achaia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"asia-g0773","name":"Asia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5}],"words":[{"base":"G0782","lemma":"ἀσπάζομαι","tr":"aspazomai","gloss":"to pay respects to","lang":"g","inPassage":17,"uses":60},{"base":"G5547","lemma":"Χριστός","tr":"Christos","gloss":"Christ","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":529},{"base":"G0027","lemma":"ἀγαπητός","tr":"agapētos","gloss":"beloved","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":61},{"base":"G3748","lemma":"ὅστις","tr":"hostis, hētis","gloss":"who","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":144},{"base":"G2872","lemma":"κοπιάω","tr":"kopiaō","gloss":"to labor","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":22},{"base":"G2962","lemma":"κύριος","tr":"kurios","gloss":"lord: God","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":714},{"base":"G1577","lemma":"ἐκκλησία","tr":"ekklēsia","gloss":"assembly","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":114},{"base":"G4773","lemma":"συγγενής","tr":"sungenēs","gloss":"kindred","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"G4904","lemma":"συνεργός","tr":"sunergos","gloss":"co-worker","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":13},{"base":"G1473","lemma":"ἐγώ","tr":"egō","gloss":"I","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":841}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CO","chapter":16,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"All the brothers here send you greetings. Greet one another with a holy kiss.","from":16},{"book":"COL","chapter":4,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Greet the brothers in Laodicea, as well as Nympha and the church that meets at her house.","from":5},{"book":"1CO","chapter":16,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The churches in the province of Asia send you greetings. Aquila and Prisca greet you warmly in the Lord, and so does the church that meets at their house.","from":5},{"book":"2CO","chapter":13,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Greet one another with a holy kiss.","from":16},{"book":"1TH","chapter":5,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Greet all the brothers with a holy kiss.","from":16},{"book":"PHM","chapter":1,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"to Apphia our sister, to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church that meets at your house:","from":5},{"book":"ROM","chapter":14,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"For whoever serves Christ in this way is pleasing to God and approved by men.","from":10},{"book":"1PE","chapter":5,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Greet one another with a kiss of love. Peace to all of you who are in Christ.","from":16}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":6},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2}]},"17-20":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":18}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G0172","lemma":"ἄκακος","tr":"akakos","gloss":"innocent","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G1370","lemma":"διχοστασία","tr":"dichostasia","gloss":"dissension","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G0185","lemma":"ἀκέραιος","tr":"akeraios","gloss":"innocent","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1578","lemma":"ἐκκλίνω","tr":"ekklinō","gloss":"to turn from","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1818","lemma":"ἐξαπατάω","tr":"exapataō","gloss":"to deceive","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G4648","lemma":"σκοπέω","tr":"skopeō","gloss":"to watch out","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G4937","lemma":"συντρίβω","tr":"suntribō","gloss":"to break","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"G5034","lemma":"τάχος","tr":"tachos","gloss":"speed","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"G2962","lemma":"κύριος","tr":"kurios","gloss":"lord: God","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":714},{"base":"G4625","lemma":"σκάνδαλον","tr":"skandalon","gloss":"stumbling block","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":15}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LUK","chapter":10,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":31,"source":"both","text":"Behold, I have given you authority to tread on snakes and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy. Nothing will harm you.","from":20},{"book":"1JN","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":25,"source":"both","text":"The one who practices sin is of the devil, because the devil has been sinning from the very start. This is why the Son of God was revealed, to destroy the works of the devil.","from":20},{"book":"JUD","chapter":1,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":22,"source":"both","text":"These are the ones who cause divisions, who are worldly and devoid of the Spirit.","from":17},{"book":"MAT","chapter":10,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"Behold, I am sending you out like sheep among wolves; therefore be as shrewd as snakes and as innocent as doves.","from":19},{"book":"2TH","chapter":3,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"Now we command you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to keep away from any brother who leads an undisciplined life that is not in keeping with the tradition you received from us.","from":17},{"book":"GEN","chapter":3,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"And I will put enmity between you and the woman, and between your seed and her seed. He will crush your head, and you will strike his heel.”","from":20},{"book":"1CO","chapter":14,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"Brothers, stop thinking like children. In regard to evil be infants, but in your thinking be mature.","from":19},{"book":"1TI","chapter":6,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":20,"source":"openbible","text":"If anyone teaches another doctrine and disagrees with the sound words of our Lord Jesus Christ and with godly teaching,","from":17}],"notes":[{"id":"gen-3-15","title":"The offspring who will crush the serpent","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[]},"21-24":{"people":[{"id":"jason-g2394","name":"Jason","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"lucius-g3066","name":"Lucius","kind":"person","brief":"Christian prophet","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"sopater-g4986","name":"Sopater","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Pyrrhus","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"timothy-g5095g","name":"Timothy","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"tertius-g5060","name":"Tertius","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"erastus-g2037","name":"Erastus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"gaius-g1050i","name":"Gaius","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"quartus-g2890","name":"Quartus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G0782","lemma":"ἀσπάζομαι","tr":"aspazomai","gloss":"to pay respects to","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":60},{"base":"G3066","lemma":"Λούκιος","tr":"Loukios","gloss":"Lucius","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2037","lemma":"Ἔραστος","tr":"erastos","gloss":"Erastus","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1050","lemma":"Γάϊος","tr":"Gaios","gloss":"Gaius","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G2394","lemma":"Ἰάσων","tr":"Iasōn","gloss":"Jason","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G3623","lemma":"οἰκονόμος","tr":"oikonomos","gloss":"manager","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"G4773","lemma":"συγγενής","tr":"sungenēs","gloss":"kindred","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"G4904","lemma":"συνεργός","tr":"sunergos","gloss":"co-worker","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"G3581","lemma":"ξένος","tr":"xenos","gloss":"foreign","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"G1992","lemma":"ἐπιστολή","tr":"epistolē","gloss":"epistle","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":24}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"He sent two of his helpers, Timothy and Erastus, to Macedonia, while he stayed for a time in the province of Asia.","from":23},{"book":"1CO","chapter":1,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I thank God that I did not baptize any of you except Crispus and Gaius,","from":23},{"book":"ACT","chapter":20,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Paul was accompanied by Sopater son of Pyrrhus from Berea, Aristarchus and Secundus from Thessalonica, Gaius from Derbe, Timothy, and Tychicus and Trophimus from the province of Asia.","from":21},{"book":"ACT","chapter":13,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now in the church at Antioch there were prophets and teachers: Barnabas, Simeon called Niger, Lucius of Cyrene, Manaen (who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch), and Saul.","from":21},{"book":"ACT","chapter":16,"verse":1,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Paul came to Derbe and then to Lystra, where he found a disciple named Timothy, the son of a believing Jewish woman and a Greek father. The brothers in Lystra and Iconium spoke well of him. Paul wanted Timothy to accompany him, so he took him and circumcised him on account of the Jews in that area, for they all knew that his father was a Greek.","from":21},{"book":"ACT","chapter":17,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The Jews, however, became jealous. So they brought in some troublemakers from the marketplace, formed a mob, and sent the city into an uproar. They raided Jasonʼs house in search of Paul and Silas, hoping to bring them out to the people.","from":21},{"book":"ACT","chapter":17,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The brothers immediately sent Paul to the coast, but Silas and Timothy remained in Berea.","from":21},{"book":"ACT","chapter":18,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And when Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul devoted himself fully to the word, testifying to the Jews that Jesus is the Christ.","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":4}]},"25-27":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"phoebe-g5402","name":"Phoebe","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27}],"places":[{"id":"cenchreae-g2747","name":"Cenchreae","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"corinth-g2882","name":"Corinth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"rome-g4514","name":"Rome","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27}],"words":[{"base":"G2596","lemma":"κατά","tr":"kata","gloss":"according to","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":472},{"base":"G0166","lemma":"αἰώνιος","tr":"aiōnios","gloss":"eternal","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":70},{"base":"G4397","lemma":"προφητικός","tr":"prophētikos","gloss":"prophetic","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G5547","lemma":"Χριστός","tr":"Christos","gloss":"Christ","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":529},{"base":"G2003","lemma":"ἐπιταγή","tr":"epitagē","gloss":"command","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"G1223","lemma":"διά","tr":"dia","gloss":"through","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":666},{"base":"G2782","lemma":"κήρυγμα","tr":"kērugma","gloss":"preaching","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"G4601","lemma":"σιγάω","tr":"sigaō","gloss":"be silent","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"G4741","lemma":"στηρίζω","tr":"stērizō","gloss":"to establish","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"G2424","lemma":"Ἰησοῦς","tr":"Iēsous","gloss":"Jesus","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":911}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CO","chapter":2,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"No, we speak of the mysterious and hidden wisdom of God, which He destined for our glory before time began.","from":25},{"book":"ROM","chapter":2,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"on the day when God will judge menʼs secrets through Christ Jesus, as proclaimed by my gospel.","from":25},{"book":"EPH","chapter":1,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"And He has made known to us the mystery of His will according to His good pleasure, which He purposed in Christ","from":25},{"book":"COL","chapter":1,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"the mystery that was hidden for ages and generations but is now revealed to His saints.","from":25},{"book":"COL","chapter":1,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"To them God has chosen to make known among the Gentiles the glorious riches of this mystery, which is Christ in you, the hope of glory.","from":25},{"book":"ISA","chapter":40,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Do you not know? Have you not heard? The LORD is the everlasting God, the Creator of the ends of the earth. He will not grow tired or weary; His understanding is beyond searching out.","from":26},{"book":"ROM","chapter":1,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Through Him and on behalf of His name, we received grace and apostleship to call all those among the Gentiles to the obedience that comes from faith.","from":26},{"book":"ROM","chapter":11,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"For from Him and through Him and to Him are all things. To Him be the glory forever! Amen.","from":27}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3}]}}